; test webmerge
; Coinductive bisimulation: three params rotate on the back-edge —
; `(p1, p2, p0)`. No slot has a uniform key across edges (phase A
; misses: `v0` vs `p_j`), and no slot is a sibling function (phase B
; misses: back-edge args are params, not structural trees). Under the
; all-equal hypothesis each slot's per-edge signature is `[V(v0),
; V(leader)]`, so p1/p2 drop to p0.
; check: block1(v1: i64):
; check-not: block1(v1: i64, v2: i64)
function %f(i64) -> i64 {
block0(v0: i64):
    jump block1(v0, v0, v0)

block1(v1: i64, v2: i64, v3: i64):
    v4 = iconst.i64 0
    v5 = icmp eq v1, v4
    brif v5, block3, block2

block2:
    jump block1(v2, v3, v1)

block3:
    v6 = iadd v2, v3
    return v6
}
